In article <1995Aug24.115933.3@geo9>, C.Leue@GeoNet.de (Christian Leue) wrote:

> Sorry if this has been asked (and answered) before: are there
> any available C-sources for Base64 encoding/decoding to generate
> MIME-compliant files for OpenVMS?
> 
> Thanks any tips!
> 
> Christian


Yes.  Via anonymous ftp to ftp.andrew.cmu.edu.  cd to /pub/mpack.  There
is C source code for unix machines which could be modified for OpenVMS. 
Also, there are compiled applications for Mac, DOS, OS/2, and Amiga.

Felix Tilley



