    I am trying to setup a modem on a DECserver 90M terminal server port
and access it via LAT for dial-in and dial-out use.  The dial-in works
and was essentially simple,  however the dial-out case is a turning out
to be a much harder task!

    I started with the FAQ by Richard Gilbert that is posted here
regularly.  I also have looked through the CD OLD in the appendix of the TSM
manual for setting up a Dial-In & Dial-Out modem.

    I have a service defined on one of the server's ports.  When I try
to set it up and connect to it I get this message:

$ MCR LATCP Create Port LTA5171: /Applic /Node=TS517 /Service=MODEM1 /NoQueue
$ Set Terminal /Perm /Modem /Dialup /Altype /hostsync LAT5171:
$ Set Host /LAT MODEM1
%LAT-F-CONFAIL, connection to MODEM1 not established
-LAT-F-LRJINUSE, port or service in use
-LAT-I-END, control returned to node xxxxx

    Yet LATCP tells me the service is both available and reachable.

$ Mcr Latcp Show Service MODEM1
Service Name:    MODEM1
Service Status:  Available
Service Ident:   5-0696 Modem
 
Node Name            Status      Rating   Identification
LAT_08002BB396B8     Reachable     90     5-0696 Modem

and TSM is also apparently happy too:

TSM> Show Service Modem1 Char
        Service: MODEM1
        Identification: 5-0696 Modem
        Ports: 1
        Rating: 90
        Enabled Characteristics: 
        Connections

    Can anyone see what I am missing or doing wrong?  What is already
using the LAT port?

    This is on an Alpha/OpenVMS v6.2 cluster.

Thanks!
rick dyson
